{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-blog-post-js","path":"/blog/2010-09-25-linq-in-asp-net/","result":{"data":{"markdownRemark":{"html":"<p>A quick sample of how to use LINQ in your webpages.</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"xml\"><pre style=\"counter-reset: linenumber NaN\" class=\"language-xml line-numbers\"><code class=\"language-xml\">&lt;% Model.ToList().ForEach(item =>\n{ %>\n  <span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">&lt;</span>tr</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">></span></span>\n      <span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">&lt;</span>td</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">></span></span>\n          &lt;%: Html.ActionLink(\"Edit\", \"Edit\", new { id = item.AlbumId })%> |\n          &lt;%: Html.ActionLink(\"Delete\", \"Delete\", new { id = item.AlbumId })%>\n      <span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">&lt;/</span>td</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">></span></span>\n      <span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">&lt;</span>td</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">></span></span>&lt;%: Html.Truncate(item.Title, 25)%><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">&lt;/</span>td</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">></span></span>\n      <span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">&lt;</span>td</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">></span></span>&lt;%: Html.Truncate(item.Artist.Name, 25)%><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">&lt;/</span>td</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">></span></span>\n      <span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">&lt;</span>td</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">></span></span>&lt;%: item.Genre.Name%><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">&lt;/</span>td</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">></span></span>\n  <span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">&lt;/</span>tr</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">></span></span>\n&lt;% }); %></code><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"line-numbers-rows\" style=\"white-space: normal; width: auto; left: 0;\"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></pre></div>\n<p>I said quick ey! :-)</p>","timeToRead":1,"excerpt":"A quick sample of how to use LINQ in your webpages. I said quick ey! :-)","frontmatter":{"title":"LINQ in ASP.NET","date":"25 September 2010","category":"Web & APIs","tags":["linq","asp.net mvc"],"image":null}}},"pageContext":{"slug":"/blog/2010-09-25-linq-in-asp-net/"}},"staticQueryHashes":["764694655"],"slicesMap":{}}